LUME>\n264.6\n\n> <PUBCHEM_COORDINATE_TYPE>\n2\n5\n10\n\n$$$$\n", "tridimensionale": true, "wikipedia_titoli": {"en": "Efinaconazole"}, "wikipedia_en": {"testo": "Efinaconazole, sold under the brand name Jublia and Clenafin among others, is a triazole antifungal compound discovered by Kaken Pharmaceutical, indicated for the treatment of onychomycosis, a fungal infection of the nail. Since it has low binding affinity with keratin, the main component of nails, it has superior nail-penetrating properties. It is approved for use in the United States, Canada, Japan and certain European countries as a 10% topical solution.", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Efinaconazole", "titolo": "Efinaconazole"}, "scheda_en": {"intro": "Efinaconazole, sold under the brand name Jublia and Clenafin among others, is a triazole antifungal compound discovered by Kaken Pharmaceutical, indicated for the treatment of onychomycosis, a fungal infection of the nail. Since it has low binding affinity with keratin, the main component of nails, it has superior nail-penetrating properties. It is approved for use in the United States, Canada, Japan and certain European countries as a 10% topical solution. \nEfinaconazole acts as a 14α-demethylase inhibitor.", "dove": "Efinaconazole is an azole antifungal indicated in the US for the topical treatment of onychomycosis of the toenails due to Trichophyton rubrum and Trichophyton mentagrophytes. Unlike nail lacquers it does not require debridement.", "storia": "Efinaconazole was discovered by Japan dermatology company Kaken Pharmaceutical. In 2014, the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) approved the New Drug Application (NDA). According to Valeant Pharmaceuticals International Inc CEO J. Michael Pearson they acquired Jublia through their purchase of Dow Pharmaceutical Sciences in 2008. Japan and Korean approvals followed. In 2024, Almirall announced completion of decentralized regulatory approval procedure for Jublia in Europe.", "titolo": "Efinaconazole", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Efinaconazole"}}